Standing Branch: chore/SCC-186-standing-push

── METHOD 1: TELL THE AGENT (RECOMMENDED) ──
Simply instruct: "Commit and push my recent file changes to main under SCC-186."
The agent syncs latest main into chore/SCC-186-standing-push, stages changed files, commits with "SCC-186 ...", pushes, opens the PR, and verifies the merge.

── METHOD 2: TERMINAL ONE-LINER ──
# 1. Switch to standing branch and pull latest main
git checkout chore/SCC-186-standing-push && git pull origin main

# 2. Stage your specific file(s)
git add path/to/file

# 3. Commit with SCC-186 summary
git commit -m "SCC-186 <your summary here>"

# 4. Push branch to GitHub
git push origin chore/SCC-186-standing-push

# 5. Open the Pull Request targeting main
gh pr create --base main --head chore/SCC-186-standing-push --title "SCC-186 <your summary here>" --body "SCC-186"

# 6. Merge the Pull Request
gh pr merge --merge

# 7. Return to main and pull latest merge
git checkout main && git pull origin main

── METHOD 3: SOURCE CONTROL UI ──

1. Bottom status bar: switch branch to chore/SCC-186-standing-push.
2. Source Control panel: click ... -> Pull, Push -> Pull from... -> origin/main.
3. Stage files with '+', enter commit message starting with SCC-186, click Commit.
4. Click 'Sync Changes' / Push.
5. Create PR on GitHub, wait for main-write-gate check (green checkmark), then click Merge pull request.
6. Switch back to main and Sync to pull the changes 
